  "name": "Big Rock Point Nuclear Power Plant",
  "scope": "Historical representative early-operation1963 Big Rock Point principal station exterior: partially buried spherical containment shell with equatorial rim/vertical outer ribs/crown walkway and exterior access ladder, tapered red-and-white striped stack, attached tall turbine hall with clerestory, lower two-storey front office/control block with deep vertical piers and glazing, shallow entrance canopy, and intrinsic low shoreward cooling-water building/short connecting service volume. Exclude interiors and process equipment, switchyard/powerlines, detached ancillary sheds, parking/roads/landscape/lake/shore riprap, people/vehicles/lettering and current spent-fuel storage/marker. Demolished station: historical-only, never default current-world.",
  "era": "Representative early operating configuration circa1963 based on undated DOE archive exterior photographs. This year is an interpretive viewing label, not the exposure date of the photographs or proof of invariant later years. Current former site is greenfield; stack removed2004, main buildings2005.",
